// docs/specs/phase3/horses-and-carts.md 3.3. One cell is 1 m x 1 m, so a part is what stands in one square metre (a cargo bed cell carries 125 kg / 250 L; a wheel is its own cell stack on the frame). A part's cargo is what its cell holds (kg and litres); needs_below lists parts one of which must lie under it in the same cell.
[
